course: dictionary
lesson: 1916
title: Come: many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Come» is a small word with many meanings, and the words around it tell you which one fits. In «Come here!» it means move towards the person speaking. In «The bus is coming» it means arrive.
explain: Look at the rest of the sentence. «Spring comes after winter» means happen in order, not move anywhere. «She comes from Ireland» means her home or her start is Ireland. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: move towards, arrive or happen. See which one still makes sense.
explain: Phrases like «come on», «come back» and «come in» often mean something a little different from the single words. In Newcastle, «howay» means «come on», so when a word or phrase is new, read the clues around it and check the dictionary if you are still stuck.
fact: Come is a verb. Its forms are come, comes, came and coming.
fact: «Come» can mean move towards the person speaking, as in «Come here!»
fact: «Come» can mean arrive or join a place, as in «The bus is coming.»
fact: «Come» can mean happen or be in an order, as in «Spring comes after winter.»
fact: «Come from» means to have a place as your home or start, as in «She comes from Ireland.»
exercise: «Come here, Sam, and look at this!» What does come mean here? | Leave the room and go away | Arrive at a shop | *Move towards the person speaking | Happen after lunch
exercise: «Spring comes after winter.» What does comes mean here? | Move towards the speaker | Arrive at a station | Stop moving | *Happen in order, one thing after another
exercise: «She comes from Ireland.» What does comes from mean? | *Has Ireland as her home or start | Is sad about Ireland | Is buying a ticket to Ireland | Is walking out of Ireland now
test: «The bus is coming, so get ready!» What does coming mean? | Going to sleep | Falling over | *Arriving here soon | Painting the bus
test: «What comes after 9?» What is the answer? | 8 | 7 | *10 | 11
exam: «Its nose was damaged long before Napoleon's soldiers came.» What does came mean? | Were sleeping | Painted the statue | Carved the rock | *Arrived at the place
